From CHBlackjack (https://github.com/bateske/CHBlackjack, Apache-2.0), by way
of CHRoulette (https://github.com/bateske/CHRoulette, Apache-2.0): the input
and frame pacing (now in the CHGame library, platform/board/arduino/CHGame/libraries/CHGame/src/
chgame/Input.*), palette, drawing, outlined lettering,
effects, sound sequencer, flash saving, debug protocol, the PC simulator and
tools, the stage's wall, and the host (the dealer from CHBlackjack's tables,
with his expressions), adapted here. The differential redraw check
(the repository's tools/chsim/diffdrive.py) and the mock-up kit
(tools/pixkit.py there) are CHRoulette's.

CHBlackjack is a derivative of "Blackjack" for the Arduboy by Press Play On
Tape - Simon Holmes (filmote), code, and Stephane C (vampirics), art
(https://github.com/Press-Play-On-Tape/Blackjack, Apache-2.0). The host is
Press Play On Tape's dealer, recoloured and retouched by hand; the 3x5 pixel
font in the CHGame library (platform/board/arduino/CHGame/libraries/CHGame/src/chgame/Draw.cpp) is
Press Play On Tape's (the ampersand was added here).

From CHChess (https://github.com/bateske/CHChess, Apache-2.0): the soft
clock ticks. From CHBackgammon (https://github.com/bateske/CHBackgammon,
Apache-2.0): the shape of the repository's tools/check.py.

The SD card reader (the CHSd library in the CHGame board package, with the
simulator's card in its host/ folder) is CHSd, the library this game shares with CHWords
and CHCrossword: HypeRunner's clean-room SPI-mode driver and FAT reader,
cut down to read-only single-block reads:

